@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;security] github-fleet-real-authorities
OAuth consent and callback MUST traverse Chromium and the packaged Marshall
provider adapter. Guest commands MUST execute in the current real KVM boot and
cross Lilly, Audi and Galileo's production authority path. No synthetic control
server, connector binding or direct credential/domain-state injection is allowed.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;privacy] github-fleet-synthetic-provider
The isolated provider MUST use fixed GitHub hostnames, valid fixture TLS and
synthetic credentials only. Logs and failure receipts MUST contain closed stage
categories and structural observations, never URLs with OAuth state/codes,
credentials, request bodies, browser documents or terminal bytes. Passing this
fixture MUST NOT be described as live GitHub or seven-family runtime evidence.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;recovery] github-fleet-detach-relocation
The GitHub journey MUST preserve browser-created machine exclusion through public
relocation to a different host and a fresh OAuth grant. Before asserting anonymous
forwarding, it MUST observe completed relocation, the admitted destination,
an advanced execution epoch and the old native unit's exit. It MUST NOT mutate
domain rows to establish those outcomes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;recovery] github-fleet-scheduled-refresh
Provider expiry alone MUST schedule refresh. The GitHub journey MUST observe real
provider calls and committed credential generations without running jobs manually
or editing SQL timestamps, phases, credentials or scheduled job arguments.
